<headroom-library version="1" id="clean-fusion-chorus" category="Clean" order="80" instrument="guitar" style="Jazz Fusion">
  <description>Wide 80s fusion polish for extended chords and legato lines: light compression into a warm big blackface, a pitch-detune chorus spread across the stereo field, a stereo ping-pong echo around 400 ms and a vintage digital hall. Neck or middle pickup; let chords ring and the repeats bloom.</description>
  <tags><tag>Clean</tag><tag>Jazz Fusion</tag><tag>Chorus</tag><tag>Stereo</tag><tag>Delay</tag><tag>Hall Reverb</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://forum.seymourduncan.com/threads/does-anyone-know-mike-sterns-rig-on-this.6201380/" title="Seymour Duncan forum: Mike Stern's rig (SPX90 pitch chorus, stereo amps)"/>
    <source url="https://gearspace.com/threads/help-im-recording-mike-stern-and-ive-got-some-questions.128255/" title="Gearspace: recording Mike Stern"/>
    <source url="https://www.jazzguitar.be/blog/jazz-guitarists-guitar-gear/" title="jazzguitar.be: famous jazz guitarists and their gear"/>
    <source url="https://www.jazzguitar.be/forum/guitar-amps-gizmos/61859-chorus-effect-jazz.html" title="jazzguitar.be forum: chorus effect in jazz"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
